read.stated_limitations:
I could not read these first-hand because the paper body was inaccessible. Two secondary sources give hints:

- **The LLM-generated digest (memgrafter; low trust)** says the paper calls out:
  - evaluation limited to textual environments, not multimodal, open-world tool-use or robotic settings;
  - higher inference-time overhead than reactive agents, with possible remedies such as WM distillation or speculative decoding;
  - compounding WM error in long rollouts ('excessive rollouts can amplify model errors') that is not quantified.
